Status: SOURCE ONLY. No compiler, syntax checker, fixture or device invocation
has been performed for these sources. No binary or installable package exists.

Files
  rescue-link.c: fixed native router helper; --monitor / --cleanup-owned only.
  controller-transient.sh: fixed .51 shell source; --setup / --cleanup-owned.
  *.in: inert unit/config/enrolment drafts, no [Install] or enable actions.
  plan-v1.json: the reviewed initial design, kept as the original contract.
  implementation-v1.json: preserved first implementation contract.
  implementation-v2.json: reviewed router fixes and separate controller blocker.

The C helper polls read-only netlink snapshots rather than subscribing to
multicast events. This reduces sequence ambiguity and needs no link/rule writes.
Each complete snapshot is bounded by a single five-second deadline; each
mutation ACK is bounded by two seconds. Stop gates prevent starting another
install after old-object cleanup, or another READY snapshot after installation.
The unit starts within300s and allows60s stop: initial wait250s plus at most
24s install/READY and19s cleanup; signal handling allows current transaction
to finish and then only exact cleanup, at most43s conservatively. It preserves other ASUS/DHCP changes:
it does not compare all normal addresses against a frozen before-image or write
them back. Only the fixed labelled address and exact peer /32 route are changed.

Initial missing/wrong-MAC/not-UP/not-carrier interfaces wait with no mutation.
Once the expected identity has been observed, a changed MAC or unknown master
is an error. Dynamic ifindex is checked together with name and enrolled MAC.
Detached eth0 does not depend on br0. On br0, normal labelled br0 IPv4 and
forwarding-state eth0 are required. No bridge state is changed by this helper.

Ownership records in a root-owned0700 /run directory precede each mutation.
Only stable ADDR/ACTIVE receipts permit automatic exact cleanup. An ambiguous
ACK, crash or readback failure leaves an intent; cleanup refuses automatic retry.
A definite address EEXIST never becomes ownership. RuntimeDirectoryPreserve=yes
preserves the evidence; no Restart loop is configured. A partial receipt may
require a later reviewed cleanup. There is no claim of a multi-message atomic
network transaction or immunity to a malicious/conflicting privileged actor.

The shell controller uses a root-only mkdir lock and atomic tmpfs receipt rename.
It does not claim filesystem fsync durability. All ip output is timeout-bounded,
stored at most65537 bytes and rejected over65536. It uses pipefail and rejects
unsupported commands, unexpected output or named protocol output rather than
guessing. Official BusyBox1.37 supports setting noprefixroute, but iproute.c omits route
protocol output. The captured .51 lacks stat as well. Consequently this original
controller shell is NOT usable as-is. It remains preserved pending a separate
private official ip-full adaptation and numeric ls metadata checks; no setup may
be attempted to discover missing capabilities. If a process
dies before releasing its mkdir lock or while an intent is pending, it refuses
automatic adoption. Cleanup only deletes the exact known peer route/address.

Additional own-object safety checks do not prove global IPv4LL uniqueness.
Before the first physical login, the controller must verify the neighbour's
Ethernet MAC02:00:00:f0:00:01 and the already enrolled native SSH host key.
No neighbour modification, ARP daemon, DAD manager, sysctl or firewall write is
introduced. Existing169.254.0.2 deveth.ai-10 remains unrelated and untouched.

Host-key public enrolment is a SEPARATE future transaction, not part of network
setup or cleanup. The .51 Dropbear client lacks UserKnownHostsFile support.
Its current native-key entry has aliases leon-ubuntu26-be19000ai and
[leon-ubuntu26-be19000ai]:2222. Port2223 requires the separate public endpoint
[leon-ubuntu26-be19000ai]:2223 with exactly the already enrolled ed25519 key from
evidence/ubuntu26/device-identity-live/ubuntu-known_hosts (fingerprint
SHA256:RfC1T1zKLkLwvjJG2t4UD3b0+z2+St0MhAumhVCrCMI). Before any later append,
require the actual global known_hosts path/parent to be trusted, root-owned,
non-symlink, the file regular with nlink1, and preserve all existing bytes.
Verify the existing comma-separated native alias against that public key; reject
conflicting2223 entries. Never read/export a private key, generate a new identity,
change warning policy, or use accept-new/TOFU. This source set does not append it.

The new listener is fixed169.254.190.15:2223 and not bound to a netdev. A topology
transition may interrupt SSH and requires reconnecting; no seamless guarantee.
Authentication remains existing native account/PAM and public key only. Ordinary
22, recovery2222, sudo policy, shadow, boot selector, guardian and ACK gates stay
unchanged. Rescue does not prove that normal LAN or ASUS is healthy.
